------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY / SURFACE VERIFICATION  (against the web source)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Data: bound via the shared P1/S8 IDrivingTemperatureStatsSource (cache-then-network GET /analytics/fleet,
  days=30, parsing drive_analytics.temperature.{inside,outside}.{min,avg,max}); the view performs no HTTP.
- Units: web useUnits -> native UnitPref; SI Celsius is converted to the user's unit ONLY at the display
  boundary (UnitConverters.TemperatureFromSi), with web safe() (null/NaN/inf -> 0) reproduced at parse.
- Six MetricCards: Inside/Outside x Min(cyan->Info)/Avg(green->Success)/Max(amber->Warning); value is the
  formatted number, the unit (°C/°F) is the subtitle, matching the web MetricCard label/value/subtitle.
- States (ALL render, none hidden): loading (skeleton grid + LiveRegion announce), loaded (six cards),
  empty (EmptyState "No temperature stats" with the thermometer glyph, web insideTemp||outsideTemp gate),
  error (QueryError + retry affordance), stale (freshness chip), offline (freshness chip + cached cells).
- Accessibility: SectionTitle + per-card Narrator names ("Inside Min: 20.0 °C"; em-dash cell "Outside Min: —"),
  loading live-region announcement, reduced-motion honoured on skeletons.
- Telemetry: view.opened slug=DrivingTemperatureStats emitted once on open (PII-safe; P1/S11).

